    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T05:52:59Z",
    "body": "Finding (SKULL issue-worker-high, not claimed): the premise does not hold on upstream/main (read at 2026-11-14, after v0.20.0).\n\n- `wire_plane_normal`, `crates/post/src/post/wire_align.rs` and `crates/app/src/post/stream.rs` do not exist on main or on any branch (`git log --all -S wire_plane_normal` is empty). No \"states no wire plane\" refusal exists anywhere in the tree.\n- A tapered wire cut posts today when the machine states its guide planes: `crates/app/tests/wire_taper.rs::a_tapered_punch_posts_its_golden_and_its_cl_shows_the_poses` drives a non-zero taper through `Generic ISO Wire EDM` on `crates/app/tests/edm/wire-iso-fixture.mch` and pins `tests/golden/nc/wire-iso/wire_taper_punch.nc` (U/V words from `app::machine::wire_edm::guide_points`). Taper by angle word (#1164, PR #1218) is also on main (`wire_taper_angle.rs`).\n- The one real refusal for a taper is `machine <m> states no edm.lower_guide_z and edm.upper_guide_z` (`app::machine::wire_edm::guide_planes`). That is the unstated-limits law of `assets/machines/AGENTS.md`: guide heights are never guessed. The Sodick ALC400G file in PR #1793 states no guide heights because no public source gives them, so its refusal is correct, not misleading.\n- No shipped `assets/machines/*.mch` is a wire EDM yet, so there is no shipped file to give a plane to; giving one a default guide height or plane would be a guess under the safety floor.\n\nSuggest closing as not a defect (no code path to fix; \"Done means\" is met by the existing taper golden for a machine that states its guides). The comment in PR #1793's `sodick_alc400g.rs` test (\"the wire plane next, #1800\") should drop the wire-plane clause there. Left open for the maintainer/main session to decide.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
